!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/scoped-host.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  The governing side of a scope push ([TSON-SCHEMA] §7.8). It deliberately does NOT import
  scoped-claim.tn: the point of `extern` is that a schema takes a value from a schema it does not
  import, the value naming its own.

  One field per cell of core's three named `scoped` instances, plus one ordinary field. `closed` is
  what makes §7.8's typed-position restriction testable -- cross-schema acceptance is authored
  intent, so a nested `!!schema` at a position the schema did not declare scoped is refused.
  """
{
  note => {
    body: text
  }

  envelope => {
    local:   declared
    foreign: extern
    either:  dynamic
    closed:  int32
  }
}
